# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/agnix/ is gitignored.
#
# TOOLCHAIN SOURCE — a tool this repo actually RUNS (#81, ingested 2026-08-02).
#
# Ray, 2026-08-19: agnix is a CRITICAL/currency dependency and this repo must
# SYNC with it. It already existed as a source and had gone SIX MINORS stale
# (v0.40.0, pinned 2026-08-02, against an installed 0.46.0) with nothing
# reporting it, because there was no `[tool.agnix]` row in `currency.toml` to
# ask. That row now exists; this pin is what it checks against.
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the version we actually run.
#   version source: mise.toml `[tools]` pin `"github:agent-sh/agnix" = "0.49.0"`,
#                   confirmed against `mise exec -- agnix --version`.
#   pinned here:    0.49.0
# A pin that drifts from the installed version makes the corpus answer questions
# about code we are not running. Not hypothetical — `sources/graphify.manifest`
# records exactly that failure: it sat two releases behind for weeks, so every
# "how does graphify work?" answer came from the wrong source. agnix adds a
# sharper edge: it runs WARNINGS-AS-ERRORS here (`mise run lint-docs` is
# `agnix . --strict`), so a rule added upstream becomes a lint FAILURE the
# moment the pin moves — v0.49.0's new CC-SET-024 is the worked example.
#
# Pin the RELEASE TAG, never a branch head — a branch drifts ahead of the release.
#
# ⚠️ TWO PROBE TRAPS LIVE ON THIS REPO'S TAGS. Both were hit on the 0.49.0 bump;
# see `[[tool.agnix.watch]]` in currency.toml and #235/#395.
#
#   1. THE TAGS ARE ANNOTATED. `git ls-remote --tags --refs` returns the TAG
#      OBJECT (`dc388699…` for v0.49.0), NOT the commit (`b0401135…`). A
#      manifest pinned to the tag object still clones, so nothing downstream
#      reports it. Control arm: graphify and datamodel-code-generator use
#      lightweight tags and both routes agree there, so the probe discriminates.
#
#   2. THE TAG LIST IS NOT VERSION-SORTED. `git ls-remote --tags` ends at
#      `v0.9.3` — three minors BEHIND v0.49.0 — and reads exactly like "latest".
#
# To bump: `mise use "github:agent-sh/agnix@<version>"`, then resolve the tag
# with mise (Ray's directive, #395) and cross-check the COMMIT:
#   mise ls-remote "github:agent-sh/agnix"
#   gh api repos/agent-sh/agnix/commits/v<version> --jq .sha
# set ref/commit here to match, then `mise run kb-build`.
#
# kind = code: AST extraction only, no LLM, no cost. NOTE this extracts the
# SOURCE and skips every .md by design — the tool's DOCS are a separate
# `kind = docs` mirror (#123), not this manifest.
url = https://github.com/agent-sh/agnix
ref = v0.49.0
commit = b0401135afa76997dd11895056a299a07d747fd0
kind = code
added = 2026-08-02
